  "reason": "The current best is config_032 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, concat) at 0.6878 acc. The strongest evidence shows scvi_n200 + multiprofile + transformer aggregation is the optimal RNA-side setup, and adding image via concat fusion provides a ~3.5% boost over RNA-only. The key remaining uncertainty is whether the fusion strategy (concat vs. weighted) can further improve performance. config_033 changes only the fusion from concat to weighted, isolating that single variable. This is the best use of experiment 8 because: (1) it is a minimal, interpretable extension of the current best, (2) if weighted fusion improves accuracy, the final experiment can combine it with a stronger image encoder (config_039, ViT-L + weighted), and (3) if it does not improve, we confirm concat is optimal and the final experiment can test ViT-L with concat (config_038) to probe whether a stronger image encoder adds value. Either outcome maximally informs the last experiment."
